Q: Foreach loop only returns the latest result from a query in laravel A: <p>you are overwriting in every loop $user variable
you can create empty array on the top of foreach, and push users to that variable</p>

<pre><code>$users = []
foreach ($conversations as $conversation) {

if ($conversation-&gt;id_participant1 !== Auth::user()-&gt;id) {

    $users[] = User::where(function ($query) use ($conversation) {
        $query-&gt;where('id', $conversation-&gt;id_participant1);
    })
        -&gt;get();
} else {
    $users[] = User::where(function ($query) use ($conversation) {
        $query-&gt;where('id', $conversation-&gt;id_participant2);
    })
        -&gt;get();
    }
}
</code></pre>

